  "edge_schema": "ledgerloop_edge_saas",
  "prompt": "Finance asks for revenue churn, not logo churn. For each month of 2025, give LedgerLoop's gross MRR churn rate: the MRR lost to churn events dated in the month divided by the MRR at the end of the month before. A churn event (event_type churn in subscription_events) carries the subscription's whole MRR as a negative mrr_delta_local; its lost MRR is that amount with the sign flipped, in euros: multiply by fx_rates.eur_per_unit for the subscription's currency on 2025-12-31. The MRR at the end of the month before is the sum of mrr_eur in mrr_monthly for the month before (mrr_monthly.month is its first day), already in euros at that rate. Contractions are not churn. Return two columns, in this order: month_start (the first day of the month) and mrr_churn_rate, as a share (0.02 for 2%), not rounded. Return one row for each month of 2025; a month with no churn shows 0. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "month_start",
        "type_class": "temporal"
      },
      {
        "name": "mrr_churn_rate",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
